# SELinux policy patches applied by `SELINUX=late lab/vm.sh <name> start` (via magiskpolicy --live)
# right before `setenforce 1`. One magiskpolicy statement per line; lines that do not apply to an
# image (unknown type) are skipped.
#
# Why: the BlissOS x86 images ship a policy that only works permissive in QEMU — with
# androidboot.selinux=enforcing they never finish booting, and a plain late `setenforce 1` crashes
# SurfaceFlinger (virgl ioctls / llvmpipe execmem), then every app's RenderThread (Mesa cannot
# enumerate /dev/dri through sysfs), then rescue-party reboots the VM.
#
# These rules ONLY cover those image/emulator gaps (graphics stack, a codec HAL mislabelled as init).
# Nothing here touches what Lindroids depends on: app <-> app unix sockets (MLS categories),
# TCP, app_data_file, execute of Termux files — those stay exactly as the image's policy says.
permissive { surfaceflinger }
permissive { hal_graphics_composer_default }
permissive { hal_graphics_allocator_default }
allow appdomain sysfs file { read open getattr }
allow appdomain sysfs dir { read open search getattr }
allow appdomain graphics_device dir { search getattr }
allow appdomain gpu_device chr_file { read write open ioctl getattr map }
allow appdomain gpu_device dir { search getattr }
allowxperm appdomain gpu_device chr_file ioctl 0x0000-0xffff
allow appdomain init binder { call transfer }
allow appdomain init fd use
